  "schema": "nfl2k5_board_kit/v1",
  "sources": [
    "Sports Video Group, 21 March 2014, 'Carolina Panthers Partner With Daktronics for Integrated LED Video System at Bank of America Stadium': 'Each end zone will feature a new LED video display measuring nearly 11,000 square feet', 56 ft high by 199 ft wide; an upper 360-degree ribbon (more than 1,900 ft) and a suite-level one (more than 2,000 ft), both about 5 ft high. Wikipedia's infobox gives 55.5 x 198.3 ft (x2).",
    "The 2026 season: the renovation's fan-facing work (new boards, seats, facade screens) begins in 2027; in 2026 the bowl stands as in 2025 (Axios, 23 July 2026, via a search summary; stadiumdb.com).",
    "The retail s04 scene (PROVED OFFLINE): the 2004 end scoreboards are housings (panthers_score01, panthers_score02 in H_group, x +-33.8, y 43.3 to 61.0, z +-119.9 to 122.6) round an 8 x 7.6 m feed quad (group32) at z +-119.8, y 46.4 to 54.1; H_group also draws the club fascia lights (LIGHT_box02) and the light banks (lite01), kept; the game's digits sit on the sideline fascias and the play clocks on the end fascias (group32), kept in place.",
    "st2's photo pose (Commons 2015, the upper deck near the +z corner; 7 points, 2.06 px) finds the far board's picture about 61 x 19 m, the published size within its far-field error; its depth reading (about z -109) is loose, so the boards stand in the retail housings' plane at z +-119.6, centred on them, their housings on the stand tops (DESIGN).",
